    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0443" n="345" xml:id="pg345"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-07-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 356.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on July 4 I
                    received your cable instruction of which a copy is inclosed,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d427-f1"/> and immediately called at the foreign office to advise
                    Her Majesty’s minister for foreign affairs of its purport. As he was not in town
                    I addressed him a note, and as he was so obliging as to accord me an interview
                    on the 5th, at 7 p.m., I waited upon him, and he expressed himself most
                    emphatically as concurring in the present policy of the United States as set
                    forth by you.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
